<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21249] Set and unset obdfilter.*.degraded for for zpool scrubs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21249</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;zpool scrubs perform heavy I/O to the pool.  Although there are mechanisms to stop or reduce scrub activity when lustre-initiated I/O is detected, they are reactive and so scrubs still affect latency and bandwidth.  In addition, user I/O competes with the scrubs and so they take longer, and scrubs sometimes trigger device failures when a device is on the edge of failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For all these reasons, it can be useful to mark OSTs in a scrubbing pool as degraded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This would essentially extend the existing ZFS zedlet which marks OSTs as degraded when device failures result in a DEGRADED zpool state.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
